{"timestamp":"2026-08-26T08:26:21.844Z","ordinal":526,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a03d2d-6b14-7ca3-ad95-4aeaf8ac734f","call_id":"call_E52IlaWp0h6OwxA58ZoY5MsO","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"# GH200 KV compression experiment handoff\n\nThis is the portable continuation context for Codex thread\n`01a032b1-ad6d-7bc2-a677-1004af67a370`.\n\n## Resume objective\n\nContinue diagnosing why the historical 92.9% Request-200 SLO result is not\nreproduced.  The next decisive experiment is an exact historical rerun with\nruntime logical dedicated KV blocks set to 2432.  Do not resume an experiment\nautomatically after restoring; verify the machine state first.\n\n## Repositories and revisions\n\n- Current tiered-serve: `/root/projects/tiered-serve`, observed HEAD `5d56a97`.\n  This worktree already had user changes; preserve them.\n- Isolated historical tiered-serve: `/root/projects/tiered-serve-af2`, commit\n  `af2e7c1`.\n- Isolated historical vLLM: `/root/projects/vllm-af2`, base commit\n  `72506c983`, with `tiered-serve-af2/patches/vllm.patch` applied.\n- Historical vLLM needed one compatibility-only Python change in\n  `vllm/entrypoints/utils.py`: construct defaults with `type(args)` rather than\n  hard-coded `EngineArgs`.  It does not touch the performance path.\n- Historical and current KV CUDA sources compared byte-for-byte equal for\n  `csrc/cache.h`, `csrc/cache_kernels.cu`, `csrc/torch_bindings.cpp`,\n  `vllm/_custom_ops.py`, and `vllm/attention/layer.py`; a rebuild was not\n  required for the completed comparisons.\n\n## Exact benchmark workload\n\n- Model: `meta-llama/Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct`\n- Config: `cao-p4-kvcomp`\n- Weight compression: `p4flat`; fused MM enabled\n- KV compression: `p4flat`\n- KV compression workers: 1\n- `max_num_batched_tokens=8192`, `max_num_seqs=512`, block size 16\n- Azure conversation dataset, 1200 requests, request rate 1.0 QPS\n- Skip first 100 and last 100; official summaries cover the middle 1000\n- Seed is fixed.  All compared runs had exactly identical per-request prompt\n  and output lengths: all-1200 totals 1,408,652 input and 250,295 output tokens;\n  middle-1000 totals 1,216,911 input and 195,841 output tokens.\n\n## Completed results\n\n| Run | Runtime logical D | Request 200 | Request 250 | TPOT p50/p90 |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| Historical recorded high, `20260817_203514` | 2432 | 92.9% | 96.2% | 154.24/185.23 ms |\n| Current code, `20260824_172838` | 2416 | 88.6% | 95.0% | 159.97/198.86 ms |\n| Historical tiered-serve + current-compatible vLLM, `20260824_190541` | 2416 | 86.4% | 94.2% | 160.27/202.53 ms |\n| Historical tiered-serve + historical vLLM, `20260824_194205` | 2416 | 85.6% | 93.5% | 161.39/204.06 ms |\n\nImportant correction: an interim 88.3% value was the all-1200 progress metric;\nthe official trimmed summary for `20260824_190541` is 86.4%.\n\nRelevant summary paths inside the experiment container:\n\n- `/root/projects/tiered-serve/logs/serving/llama_3_1_70b_instruct/cao-p4-kvcomp/20260817_203514/summary.csv`\n- `/root/projects/tiered-serve/logs/serving/llama_3_1_70b_instruct/cao-p4-kvcomp/20260824_172838/summary.csv`\n- `/root/projects/tiered-serve-af2/logs/serving/llama_3_1_70b_instruct/cao-p4-kvcomp/20260824_190541/summary.csv`\n- `/root/projects/tiered-serve-af2/logs/serving/llama_3_1_70b_instruct/cao-p4-kvcomp/20260824_194205/summary.csv`\n\n## Runtime evidence\n\n- Historical high: HBM available 21.29 GiB, logical D=2432, tail=512,\n  physical HBM rows=2944, offloadable capacity=14561.\n- Current run: HBM available 21.19 GiB, logical D=2416, physical rows=2928.\n- Fully historical rerun: HBM available 21.30 GiB, logical D=2416,\n  physical rows=2928, offloadable capacity=14561.\n- Therefore the latest comparison was intentionally fixed to the current run's\n  D=2416 and was not yet an exact reproduction of the 92.9% run's D=2432.\n\nOffloadable KV occupancy snapshots:\n\n- Historical high: mean 467.2, median 319.5, p90 1230.5, max 2610 blocks,\n  positive in 76.2% of snapshots.\n- Current: mean 581.7, median 434.5, p90 1530, max 2743, positive 81.0%.\n- Fully historical D=2416 rerun: mean 612.9, median 444, p90 1442,\n  max 2969, positive 82.5%.\n\nDecode scheduler step medians were approximately 105.2 ms for the historical\nhigh, 110.6 ms for current, and 110.5 ms for the fully historical rerun.\nHigher service time causes more concurrent active requests, which raises KV\noffloading and creates positive feedback.  This describes the observed path but\ndoes not yet identify the first cause.\n\nHistorical runs also showed large dispersion even at the same capacity:\nruntime D=2448 produced Request-200 results from 81.4% to 91.9%.  Do not treat\nthis as permission to dismiss the gap as noise; exact D=2432 repeated trials\nare still required.\n\n## Memory and boot findings\n\n- A failed CUDA context once left about 4.3 GiB HBM allocated without a process\n  shown by `nvidia-smi`.  Stopping `nvidia-persistenced` cleared it.  Restarting\n  persistence alone consumed 0 MiB, so the daemon was not itself the allocation.\n- Correct clean-boot order used: mount `/mnt/hugepages` as 16-GiB hugetlbfs,\n  ensure 23 hugepages, set/verify GPU persistence, 900 W power limit, and\n  1980 MHz application clock, then start the existing `tiered-serve` container.\n- `launch.sh` is destructive setup: it imports the image and recreates the\n  container.  Do not run it merely to restart the existing container.\n- The shutdown message `Error removing directory /mnt/hugepages: Device or\n  resource busy` is a cleanup bug caused by trying to `rmdir` the hugetlbfs\n  mount point; it is not the primary server failure.\n- Before the backup request, an exact-D=2432 rerun had just begun loading but\n  was explicitly interrupted.  Verify no server process, idle GPU HBM, and all\n  hugepages free before any new experiment.\n\n## Next experiment\n\nReproduce the historical high exactly:\n\n1. Verify HBM is clean, persistence enabled, power limit 900 W, clock 1980 MHz,\n   `/mnt/hugepages` is hugetlbfs, and all 23 pages are free.\n2. Use historical tiered-serve `af2e7c1` and historical vLLM base `72506c983`\n   plus its patch.\n3. Old-code environment-variable semantics include the 512 resident-tail rows.\n   Set `TIERED_SERVE_DEDICATED_KV_BLOCKS=2944` to obtain runtime logical\n   `num_dedicated_blocks=2432`.  Do not confuse the environment value with the\n   scheduler-visible logical D.\n4. Keep worker=1, weight hugepages=14, weight buffers=2, address order=0,\n   p4flat/p4flat, fused MM, and the exact benchmark above.\n5. Confirm from startup logs: HBM ~21.29 GiB, logical D=2432, tail=512,\n   physical offset=2944, offloadable=14561.\n6. Run at least three clean repetitions and compare the median, including\n   offload occupancy and scheduler-step distributions.\n\n## Continuation instruction\n\nOn a fresh machine, clone branch `gh200`, give this document and\n`visible-transcript.md` to Codex, and ask:\n\n> Read the GH200 handoff and visible transcript, verify the restored repository\n> paths and machine state, then continue from the exact historical D=2432\n> experiment. Do not rerun anything until the preflight checks pass.\n\"\"\"P4Flat KV cache compressor.\n\nDrop-in ``kv_compressor`` for ``DualMemoryLoader`` that uses the BF16 P4-flat\ncodec (per-64x64-tile 16-entry exponent palette + 4-bit code + raw\nsign|mantissa byte, with out-of-palette exponents kept as an exception list).\nSelected with ``--kv-comp p4flat`` (``TIERED_SERVE_KV_COMP_BACKEND=p4flat``).\n\nLike :class:`DietGPUKVCompressor` the base :class:`P4FlatKVCompressor` is a\nGPU-kernel backend (no C++ worker threads): ``compress_batch_async`` launches\nthe compress + D2H on an internal CUDA stream and ``wait_compress_async``\nsynchronises it.  It serves the ``gpu_direct`` KV producer mode (the default\nfor ``--kv-comp p4flat``).  The ``cpu_after_raw_swap`` producer is served by\nthe :class:`P4FlatCPUKVCompressor` subclass below (CPU worker-pool encode);\nboth share the same GPU decode kernel and on-host storage layout.\n\nIt subclasses :class:`DietGPUKVCompressor` purely to reuse the codec-agnostic\npersistent-slot bookkeeping (``_assign_kv_slot`` / ``_free_kv_slot`` /\n``has_*`` / ``free_persistent_block`` / ``decompress_batch`` chunking).  The\nstorage layout and the codec are completely different and overridden below.\n\nStorage layout (per layer, per K and V), one dense pool of variable-length\ncompressed blobs indexed by physical slot:\n  - ``blob``       : pinned [host_n, max_comp_size] uint8.  Each row holds a\n    serialised compressed block ``[headers | codes | sm | codec |\n    exc_idx | exc_val]`` (or, on raw fallback, the raw BF16 bytes).\n  - ``total_size`` : pinned [host_n] int32 — used bytes of the blob row.\n  - ``exc_cnt``    : pinned [host_n] int32 — number of exceptions.\n  - ``is_raw``     : pinned [host_n] uint8 — 0 compressed, 1 raw BF16 stored\n    in-row, 2 raw BF16 retained only in secondary KV (tight-stride overflow).\n\nA KV block of shape ``block_shape`` is flattened to ``block_numel`` BF16\nelements and reshaped to a 2-D ``[M_b, K_b]`` matrix with both dims multiples\nof 64 (p4flat requires this).  The reshape is a contiguous view, so the codec\nstays bit-exact; the (M_b, K_b) factoring only affects the compression ratio.\n``block_numel`` must therefore be a multiple of 64*64 = 4096.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport ctypes\nimport ctypes\nimport glob\nimport heapq\nimport logging\nimport os\nimport queue\nimport threading\nimport time\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Tuple\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport torch\n\nfrom tiered_serve.compressor_base import TensorCompressor\nfrom tiered_serve.dietgpu_kv_compressor import DietGPUKVCompressor\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(\"vllm\")  # configured/flushed handler (was __name__\n# = \"tiered_serve.*\" -> root, which suppressed INFO and split ERROR to stderr,\n# hiding [kv-decode]/MAPPING-DESYNC diagnostics from the server log file)\n_ENV_KV_DETAILED_NVTX = (\n    os.getenv(\"TIERED_SERVE_KV_DETAILED_NVTX\", \"0\") == \"1\")\n\ntry:\n    from tiered_serve.cpp_exts import zipserv_p4flat_ext as _p4f_ext\n    _HAS_P4FLAT = True\nexcept Exception as _e:  # pragma: no cover - extension build/runtime issue\n    logger.warning(\n        \"P4FlatKVCompressor disabled: failed to load zipserv_p4flat_ext \"\n        \"(%s: %s)\", type(_e).__name__, _e)\n    _p4f_ext = None\n    _HAS_P4FLAT = False\n\ndef _align(n: int, a: int) -> int:\n    return (n + a - 1) // a * a\n\n\ndef _factor_64(numel: int) -> Tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Factor ``numel`` into ``(M_b, K_b)`` with both multiples of 64,\n    chosen as close to square as possible.  Raises if ``numel`` is not a\n    multiple of 4096 (= 64*64).\"\"\"\n    if numel % 4096 != 0:\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"P4Flat KV: block_numel={numel} is not a multiple of 4096 \"\n            f\"(64*64); cannot factor into 64-aligned (M_b, K_b). Padding is \"\n            f\"not supported.\")\n    best = None\n    m = 64\n    while m * m <= numel:\n        if numel % m == 0:\n            k = numel // m\n            if k % 64 == 0:\n                best = (m, k)  # largest square-ish m wins as loop advances\n        m += 64\n    if best is None:\n        # Fall back to the most rectangular valid split (M_b=64).\n        if (numel // 64) % 64 == 0:\n            best = (64, numel // 64)\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(\n                f\"P4Flat KV: cannot factor block_numel={numel} into \"\n                f\"64-aligned (M_b, K_b).\")\n    return best\n\n\ndef _factor_64_kv(numel: int, occupancy: bool) -> Tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Factor a KV block into ``(M_b, K_b)``.\n\n    Occupancy mode (``TIERED_SERVE_KV_P4FLAT_OCCUPANCY``) lays the block out\n    *tall* — ``K_b=64`` so ``M_b=numel//64`` — instead of square.  The KV\n    block is ``[block_size, H, D]`` flattened row-major, so the token axis is\n    the outermost (slowest) dim: written tokens occupy a contiguous *prefix*\n    of rows and the unwritten tail is a contiguous suffix of all-zero rows.\n    A tall layout maximises the number of independent 64-row palette-tile\n    bands (``M_b//64``), making the all-zero suffix fall on whole skippable\n    tile bands at the finest possible granularity (``4096//H/D`` tokens/band).\n    A square factoring would instead pack ~8 tokens into one 64-row band (or\n    a single band for small blocks, ``M_b==64``), defeating partial-block\n    skipping.  Tile count — and thus palette/header overhead — is identical\n    either way (``numel//4096`` tiles), so the ratio impact is marginal.\n\n    Non-occupancy mode keeps the historical square factoring (bit-exact with\n    the validated path).\"\"\"\n    if not occupancy:\n        return _factor_64(numel)\n    if numel % 4096 != 0:\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"P4Flat KV: block_numel={numel} is not a multiple of 4096; \"\n            f\"cannot use occupancy-aware tall layout.\")\n    return (numel // 64, 64)\n\n\nclass P4FlatKVCompressor(DietGPUKVCompressor):\n    \"\"\"BF16 P4-flat KV cache compressor (GPU-kernel backend).\"\"\"\n\n    # The GPU-encode path uses the batched-compress pinned staging; the\n    # CPU-encode subclass overrides this to skip allocating it.\n    _USES_GPU_COMPRESS = True\n\n    def __init__(self, comp_stream: torch.cuda.Stream):\n        if not _HAS_P4FLAT:\n            raise RuntimeError(\n                \"P4FlatKVCompressor requires tiered-serve's zipserv_p4flat_ext \"\n                \"extension to build successfully.\")\n        # Bypass DietGPUKVCompressor.__init__ (it loads DietGPU and allocates\n        # an ANS workspace we don't need); initialise the shared state directly.\n        TensorCompressor.__init__(self, comp_stream=comp_stream)\n        self.comp_stream = comp_stream\n        self.batch_decomp_stream = torch.cuda.Stream(priority=0)\n        # One-stream KV decode: when set, the loader points batch_decomp_stream\n        # at exec_stream so the decode (H2D + kernels + breakdown events) runs on\n        # the compute stream — used as a plain attribute, no per-call resolution.\n        self._kv_decode_on_compute = os.getenv(\n            \"TIERED_SERVE_KV_DECODE_ON_COMPUTE\", \"0\") == \"1\"\n        # KV-load stream separation: run the compressed-blob H2D on the\n        # dedicated load_kv_stream (wired by the loader) instead of\n        # batch_decomp_stream, with a 2-slot blob ring so layer L+1's H2D\n        # pipelines with layer L's decode.  load_kv_stream is gated on\n        # \"QKV weights loaded\" by the graph wrapper, so the blob H2D starts\n        # when the single copy engine is free of weight H2D — otherwise it\n        # queues behind weight and the _kv_h2d_begin.._kv_dec_h2d interval\n        # absorbs that wait (small-batch KVLoad read ~= WLoad).  Decode\n        # kernels stay on batch_decomp_stream (what exec's attn barrier waits\n        # on).  Always on — the blob H2D runs on load_kv_stream whenever the\n        # loader wires one (it aliases it to load_weight_stream), and falls back\n        # to the single-stream fused H2D+decode only when no load_kv_stream is\n        # wired (e.g. a standalone compressor with no loader).\n        self.load_kv_stream = None   # wired by the loader after construction\n        self._dec_blob_ring_idx = 0\n        self._kv_split_h2d_enabled = (\n            os.getenv(\"TIERED_SERVE_KV_NO_SPLIT\", \"0\") != \"1\")\n        # Set by the loader from time_breakdown.  When False, the decode skips\n        # the breakdown-only event records (_kv_h2d_begin) — the per-step CUDA\n        # event record() was ~12% of forward-thread CPU in profiling.\n        self._tb = False\n\n        # Per-decode metadata (slots / valid_rows / exc_cnt / is_raw) H2D.\n        # Default = async ring of pinned buffers, event-gated so a lagging\n        # in-flight H2D is never overwritten on reuse — the exact failure that\n        # forced the old synchronous ``torch.stack(...).cuda()`` (pageable ->\n        # ~1 ms/graph CPU dispatch that starves the GPU).  Set\n        # TIERED_SERVE_KV_META_SYNC=1 to restore that legacy sync path.\n        self._meta_sync_fallback = os.getenv(\n            \"TIERED_SERVE_KV_META_SYNC\", \"0\") == \"1\"\n        self._meta_ring_n = 0\n        self._meta_ring_pi = None   # list[pinned int32 [5*cap]]  (cs,vrk,eck,vrv,ecv)\n        self._meta_ring_pu = None   # list[pinned uint8 [2*cap]]  (is_raw k,v)\n        self._meta_ring_b = None    # list[pinned int64 [cap]]    (block_ids)\n        self._meta_ring_ev = None   # list[cuda.Event] gating buffer reuse\n        self._meta_ring_idx = 0\n\n        # Reused, codec-agnostic persistent-slot bookkeeping (see base class).\n        self._compressed_kv: Dict[int, Any] = {}\n        self._persistent_valid: Dict[int, bytearray] = {}\n        self._kv_slot: Dict[int, torch.Tensor] = {}\n        self._kv_slot_np: Dict[int, Any] = {}   # numpy authority (shared mem)\n        self._kv_slot_block: Dict[int, List[int]] = {}\n        # P4Flat free-list slot management (overrides the base dense\n        # swap-with-last).  ``_kv_active_count`` is repurposed as the staging\n        # HIGH-WATER-MARK (max-assigned-slot + 1 = the [0:hwm] extent the decode\n        # H2D copies); freed slots go to a per-layer min-heap and are refilled\n        # lowest-first so hwm — hence the decode over-copy — stays tight, and\n        # top-of-range frees shrink hwm.  This makes ``free`` metadata-only (no\n        # _move_host_slot host memcpy, no decode-stream sync) — see\n        # ``_free_kv_slot`` and ``_kv_free_metadata_only`` below.\n        self._kv_active_count: Dict[int, int] = {}   # == hwm per layer\n        self._kv_free_heap: Dict[int, list]